  "helpCommonQuestions": "Common questions",
  "helpFaqLogFoodQ": "How do I log what I ate?",
  "helpFaqLogFoodA": "On the Today tab, tap \"Add\" next to the meal (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner or Snacks). Search for the food, enter how many grams you ate and tap \"Add\". You can also scan a barcode on the Foods tab.",
  "helpFaqNoScaleQ": "I don't weigh my food. What should I enter?",
  "helpFaqNoScaleA": "A rough guess is fine. A slice of bread is about 30 g, an apple about 150 g, a cup of cooked rice about 160 g and a chicken breast about 170 g. Use the quick buttons (50, 100, 150, 200 g) as a starting point.",
  "helpFaqKcalLeftQ": "What does \"kcal left\" mean?",
  "helpFaqKcalLeftA": "It is how many more calories you can eat today and still stay on track for your goal. If you go over, the number turns red. One day over is fine; what matters is most days.",
  "helpFaqMacrosQ": "What are protein, carbs and fat?",
  "helpFaqMacrosA": "They are the three nutrients that give food its calories. Protein helps build and repair muscle, carbs are your main energy source, and fat supports your body in many ways. Focus on calories first, then on getting enough protein.",
  "helpFaqCalorieGoalQ": "How is my daily calorie goal worked out?",
  "helpFaqCalorieGoalA": "From your age, weight, height, gender and how active you are, we estimate how many calories you burn on a normal day. Then we take away 500 to lose weight, add 300 to build muscle, or keep it the same. Exercise you log is added on top for that day.",
  "helpFaqLogExerciseQ": "How do I log exercise?",
  "helpFaqLogExerciseA": "Go to the Workouts tab. In Simple mode, find the activity (walking, cycling, …), tap it, choose how many minutes and tap \"I did this\".",
  "helpFaqAdvancedModeQ": "What is Advanced mode?",
  "helpFaqAdvancedModeA": "Advanced mode is for planning gym workouts week by week. If you are new, choose a ready-made plan: Full Body is 3 days a week and we fill in the exercises for you.",
  "helpFaqChangeGoalQ": "How do I change my weight or goal?",
  "helpFaqChangeGoalA": "Go to the Me tab and tap the edit button at the top. To track your weight over time, use \"Weight log\" on the same tab.",
  "helpDisclaimer": "Calorie goals, calories burned and BMI in this app are estimates to guide you, not medical advice. If you have a health condition, are pregnant, or plan a big change in diet or exercise, check with a doctor first.",
